      "reviewId": "BV-1-33829737",
      "text": "This restaurant is a gem. Me and my husband were looking for something out of the \"ordinary\". We truly found it! Between the food and ambiance, I truly felt like I was in a Parisian bistro! I had the Seafood Bouillabaisse- to die for!- and my husband had Chicken Tagine- it was also outstanding- and we are truly hard to impress. The wine selection was ample and modestly priced. Also glad we left room for dessert because the owner's wife, who charmingly took care of our table, makes them fresh daily. The chef, came out to greet our table. There, we found out that the restaurant was owned and operated by them. This delightful Eurpean couple gave us a tour of the garden patio they constructed themselves- wow! Can't wait to go back.",
