      "reviewId": "BV-1-33677246",
      "text": "We were visiting from North Carolina for a week and found this amazing French Restaurant while walking around the streets of our resort. The owner/chef was extremely friendly and came to our table and introduced himself. His wife, our server, was very sweet and extremely attentive. My boyfriend had the lamb chops and I had the sea bass and both were delicious! We also shared the meatball appetizer and the fig duck sausage appetizer, which also were mouth watering! The Pinot Noir we had was the best we ever had! The atmosphere was very romantic and this was truly a wonderful dining experience. You definitely have to make this a priority when visiting the South Beach area!",
